# Communication

Canonical: `rules/08-communication-style.md`. Templates: `skills/communicate-briefly.md`.

Short. Direct. Concrete. Visible. Default 1–5 short lines.

Name the exact thing — file, function, command, test, error, count, blocker.
`auth.service.ts:41 — refreshToken() returns 401.` not "something went wrong".

| Situation | Format                                        |
| --------- | --------------------------------------------- |
| Working   | `Working — <task>.`                           |
| Progress  | `~<n>/100. Done: <x>. Left: <y>.`             |
| Blocked   | `Blocked: <exact reason>.`                    |
| Failure   | `<thing> failed: <exact error>. <next step>.` |
| Tests     | `<suite>: <passed>/<total> passed.`           |
| Finished  | `Done. <proof>.`                              |

- A blocker starts with `Blocked:` and fits in two lines.
- `Done.` carries evidence — a passing suite, a green build, a verified flow.
- No filler openers (`Certainly`, `Let me explain`, `It is worth noting`).
- Never claim background work unless it is genuinely running.
- Every status line carries new information.
